#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""floor_dfpn — exact MMAE floor prover for DEEP-graph ARC-AGI-3 demo levels.

Two ported techniques (offline whitebox floor-finding, NOT the shipped solver):

  (1) DEPTH-FIRST PROOF-NUMBER SEARCH / iterative-deepening (df-pn, single-agent
      form = IDA* with a transposition table). We frame floor-finding as proving
      the predicate  P(d) := "a win exists within d moves"  for increasing d.
      For a fixed bound d a depth-first search PROVES P(d) (finds a <=d win) or
      DISPROVES it (exhausts every state with f = g + h <= d and finds none, so
      floor > d). The smallest d that is PROVEN true is the EXACT floor. Unit move
      cost + integer admissible h => the only thresholds that matter are the
      integers d = h(start), h(start)+1, ... so iteration d is exactly "prove
      P(d)". A transposition table (min-g-per-state, this iteration) shares the
      enormous number of transpositions on these deep graphs; because a win state
      has h = 0 (f = its depth) and a consistent h keeps f non-decreasing along
      every path, iteration d provably visits every <=d win -> disproof of d is a
      real proof floor > d.

  (2) DERIVED ADMISSIBLE STATE-ABSTRACTION. h(s) is a SOUND lower bound on
      moves-to-win, computed on the engine's OWN state (whitebox), never pixels:
        - nav (g50t / dc22 / lf52 agent leg): manhattan(agent_cell, goal_cell);
        - paint-coverage (re86): a function of the still-unpainted target cells;
        - push (lf52 box leg): min-cost matching of box cells to target cells.
      Admissibility is a THEOREM given two per-game facts, both re-verified against
      the live engine here: (i) h = 0 on every winning state; (ii) every legal
      move changes h by at most `move_bound` (consistency). (i)+(ii) => h(s) <=
      dist(s) by induction, so h(start) is itself an instant lower bound and h
      soundly prunes the df-pn search. A RUNTIME assertion checks (ii) on every
      expanded edge; ANY violation VOIDS the 'proven' verdict and the level is
      reported as a lower/upper bound pair instead.

Soundness contract:
  - 'proven' is emitted ONLY when df-pn disproves d = floor-1 AND proves d = floor
    (the searched f<=floor-1 region is fully exhausted, not budget-truncated) AND
    the consistency assertion never fired AND the winning route replay-verifies at
    exactly `floor` moves on a FRESH engine restore.
  - Otherwise the level is 'ub': LB = the tightest disproven-depth+1 (df-pn) or
    h(start) (abstraction), UB = shortest replay-verified winning route. Clearly
    labelled 'ub', not 'proven'.

Reuses tools/mmae_minimum.py: init_replay_backend / restore / act / frame_of /
lc_of / whitebox_sig (complete Markov key) / acquire_level_starts / resolve_game_id
/ verify_replay. Deterministic: node-bounded, fixed action order, no wall-clock in
the proof logic.

Usage:
  python3 tools/floor_dfpn.py --game g50t --levels 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 \
      --cache-starts <path>/g50t_starts.pkl --nodes 4000000 \
      --json <path>/g50t_dfpn.json
"""
